w4v|v|An association of men belonging to the same class, or engaged in kindred pursuits, formed for mutual aid and protection; a business fraternity or corporation; as, the Stationers' Guild; the Ironmongers' Guild. They were originally licensed by the government, and endowed with special privileges and authority. ; A guildhall. ; A religious association or society, organized for charitable purposes or for assistance in parish work.	o:20f9,69,3~20f9,69,3
