w5g|a|Having incurred guilt; criminal; morally delinquent; wicked; chargeable with, or responsible for, something censurable; justly exposed to penalty; -- used with of, and usually followed by the crime, sometimes by the punishment. ; Evincing or indicating guilt; involving guilt; as, a guilty look; a guilty act; a guilty feeling. ; Conscious; cognizant. ; Condemned to payment.	j:eyn,80,4;19ou,18,1;1hwv,13,3~eyn,80,4;1hwv,13,3;19ou,18,1	e:210s,46,3;1mex,42,1;qod,33,5;x5,13,5~x5,13,5;qod,33,5;210s,46,3;1mex,42,1
w5i|n|A district on the west coast of Africa (formerly noted for its export of gold and slaves) after which the Guinea fowl, Guinea grass, Guinea peach, etc., are named. ; A gold coin of England current for twenty-one shillings sterling, or about five dollars, but not coined since the issue of sovereigns in 1817.	a:p3p,154,1~p3p,154,1	n:1cdz,50,3~1cdz,50,3	N:1iue,151,4~1iue,151,4
